    "carry_forward": [
      "Restate the incremental-write rule inside the brief, not just in Arch's own context. The gate printed it at loop start and it still cost a 59-tool-call turn, because the agent reading the brief never saw it. Naming it in the assignment is the difference between a standing rule and an applied one.",
      "Size a dispatch --timeout from the work the brief actually asks for, and count the waiting: four capture replays plus a fresh suite is twenty-plus minutes of measurement before a single word of report, and the agent will also burn its own clock on sleep-and-poll loops against its background jobs.",
      "A voided final-verification receipt does not necessarily cost another suite run. Re-running final_verification.py after a signature-changing edit to the closeout record returned REUSED EVIDENCE in about a minute, rebinding the existing intact execution to the new review_signature. Try the re-run before planning around an eleven-minute suite."
    ],
